  "body": "## What changed\n\nEach catalog case has separate `regenerates` and `rebuilds` tests.\nThe five cases now have ten independent workflow results.\nThe suite has 16 tests, up from five. No test is ignored.\nEach workflow has a 60-second wall-clock budget.\nEach workflow prints its name, elapsed time, and budget, including when it fails.\nShared assertions move to a helper module. Both source files stay below 400 lines.\nEach rebuild removes only its own scratch directory.\nThe existing NC comparisons and portability checks remain in place.\n\n## Cause\n\nTwo loops ran all cases inside two tests.\nThe first failed assertion stopped each loop.\nThe tests did not measure or limit each case.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins:\n\n- `contract::every_case_has_two_named_test_results` checks both workflow names for every discovered case.\n- `contract::two_broken_cases_report_both_names_and_times` checks two named failures and their times in each workflow.\n- `support::a_case_over_its_budget_fails_by_name` checks a named timeout and its heavy-lane guidance.\n\nThe first two pins failed on unchanged upstream/main `61a817bed` before the fix.\nBoth pass with the fix.\nThe budget pin passes with a 1 ms limit and a 50 ms worker.\n\nMutation checks:\n\n- Restoring the original file and retaining the contract pins makes both pins fail. Restoring the fix makes both pass.\n- Replacing `recv_timeout` with unbounded `recv` makes the budget pin fail. Restoring the timeout makes it pass.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passes all 16 tests.\nAll ten workflows run in debug mode. Their times range from 0.256 to 12.415 seconds in the gate.\nThe first full debug run took at most 21.617 seconds for a case.\nAll cases stay below the budget, so none moves to the heavy lane.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passes.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe release heavy lanes, UI, and a real machine did not run.\nA real hanging model did not run. The timeout pin uses a sleeping worker.\nThe timeout bounds the test result. It cannot cancel the worker thread.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n#2913 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nIt adds `slots_case_posts_a_slot_and_a_trochoidal_slot_to_the_same_floor` and its helper.\nIt does not change the two loops replaced here.\nIts new catalog case will also need two workflow tests when the changes combine.\n\nChangelog: none (test structure and timing only)\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #2857\n",
